    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Overbite vs Underbite: Causes, Treatments, and How to Fix Them"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Have you ever wondered why some people's teeth don't align properly when they bite down? Whether it's an overbite or an underbite, misaligned teeth can affect more than just appearance. You might not think it's a big deal, but bite issues can lead to serious dental and even health problems. So, what exactly is the difference between an overbite and an underbite, and why does it matter?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "There are some forms of malocclusion, or improper bite alignment, which includes overbite and underbite conditions. Let’s dive deeper into these conditions, understand the causes, and see how they can be treated."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "What is the Difference Between Overbite vs Underbite?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In simple terms, an overbite happens when your upper teeth overlap too much with your lower teeth, while an underbite occurs when the lower teeth sit in front of the upper teeth. Both can cause discomfort, difficulty in chewing, and even jaw pain over time."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Understanding the distinction between overbite vs underbite is crucial for determining the right treatment. Each condition has different underlying causes and, thus, may require unique approaches. But before we get into the details of treatment, let's explore the root causes of these bite issues."
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "../assets/blog/shared/orthodontic-illustration-02.png",
      "alt": "Are braces faster than Invisalign",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Causes of Overbite vs Underbite"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Both overbites and underbites can be caused by a mix of genetic and environmental factors. Here’s a closer look:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Genetics: If your parents or grandparents had an overbite or underbite, there’s a good chance you might have one too. Genetic factors influence the size and shape of your jaw and teeth, which can lead to misalignment, and jaw discrepancies.."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Childhood Habits: Thumb-sucking, prolonged pacifier use, or prolonged bottle-feeding can all cause alignment issues. When these habits continue beyond the age of five, they may alter the natural growth of the jaw, leading to an overbite or underbite."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Jaw Injuries: Trauma to the jaw can shift teeth and cause bite problems. A severe accident might misalign the upper or lower jaw, resulting in underbite vs overbite , or crossbite issues."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Tumours: Rarely, tumours in the jawbone can cause one part of the jaw to grow at an abnormal rate, leading to bite issues."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "As you can see, overbite vs underbite is more than just a cosmetic concern—it can be a serious dental issue that affects overall oral health."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "How to Diagnose Overbite vs Underbite"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It’s pretty easy for a dentist or orthodontist to diagnose an overbite or underbite. They’ll perform a visual exam and take X-rays or dental impressions to assess how your teeth fit together. In some cases, they might even use 3D imaging for a more detailed look. Here’s a table that breaks down the common diagnostic methods for overbite vs underbite:"
    },
    {
      "type": "th",
      "text": "Diagnostic Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "th",
      "text": "Purpose"
    },
    {
      "type": "th",
      "text": "Time Required"
    },
    {
      "type": "th",
      "text": "Cost"
    },
    {
      "type": "th",
      "text": "Accuracy Level"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Visual Exam"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Basic assessment of bite and alignment"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "5-10 minutes"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Low"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "High"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "X-rays"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Checks bone structure and tooth position"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "10-15 minutes"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Moderate"
    },
    {
