    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Measures facial structure and jaw alignment"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "10-15 minutes"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "Moderate to High"
    },
    {
      "type": "td",
      "text": "High"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Once diagnosed, the next step is finding the right treatment to correct the bite issue."
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "../assets/blog/shared/orthodontic-illustration-03.png",
      "alt": "Are braces faster than Invisalign",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Treatment Options for Overbite vs Underbite"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The good news is, whether you have an overbite or an underbite, there are several effective treatment options. These treatments range from non-invasive to surgical, depending on the severity of your condition."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Braces or Aligners"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Braces and clear aligners are the most common ways to correct both overbites and underbites. They work by gradually shifting your teeth into the correct position over time. Here’s a quick breakdown of braces vs aligners:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Braces can be more effective for severe cases."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Aligners are more comfortable but are better suited for mild to moderate issues."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Treatment duration varies, but most cases take 1-2 years to correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Jaw Surgery"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In extreme cases, especially for severe underbites, jaw surgery may be necessary. This procedure realigns the jaw to ensure a proper bite. Though it's more invasive, it can provide permanent relief from bite-related problems."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Dental Appliances"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Some patients with mild overbite or underbite issues can benefit from dental appliances like retainers or headgear. These devices help shift teeth and correct alignment without the need for braces or surgery."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Bullet Points of Additional Treatment Options:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Tooth reshaping: Adjusts the shape of teeth for minor overbites."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Extraction: Removes overcrowded teeth to make room for proper alignment."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Veneers: Cosmetic option for covering minor imperfections of the teeth."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Palate expanders: Widens the upper jaw to correct underbites."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Botox: For severe jaw pain caused by overbite or underbite, Botox injections can relax the muscles."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "With the right treatment plan, correcting your bite is entirely possible. Consulting with an orthodontist early on can make a world of difference in avoiding long-term complications."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Effects of Ignoring Overbite vs Underbite"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "What happens if you leave an overbite or underbite untreated? Well, the results are often far more than cosmetic. Ignoring these issues can lead to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Jaw pain or TMJ disorders"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Headaches and neck strain"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Difficulty chewing and speaking"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Tooth wear and tear"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Increased risk of cavities or gum disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The sooner you address these bite issues, the better your overall dental health will be. So, don’t delay in seeking treatment for overbite vs underbite concerns."
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Final Thoughts"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Fixing an overbite or underbite isn’t just about having a perfect smile—it’s about ensuring long-term oral health. The causes of these issues can vary, but treatments today are highly effective, whether you opt for braces, aligners, or surgery. If you’ve been struggling with bite problems, now is the time to take action."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Consult a dental professional today to explore your options and find the right solution for overbite vs underbite."
    },
